# English-Only Developer Text & Localized UI Copy

## Comments

- Write **all** new and edited **comments** in **English**: `//`, `/* */`, `///` dartdoc/JSDoc, docstrings, SQL comments, and inline explanations.
- Do **not** use Arabic or any non-English language in code comments, `TODO`/`FIXME` notes, or developer annotations inside source files.
- Keep comments **minimal and purposeful** — explain non-obvious *why*, and remove redundant, obvious, or stale comments in any code you touch (see **`engineering-quality.mdc`**).

## User-Facing Strings

- **User-facing strings** must **never** be hardcoded in views or components — neither English nor Arabic.
- **Mobile / Flutter:** route every UI string through `AppLocalizations` / ARB files (`app_en.arb` + `app_ar.arb`, or project locale files). See **`mandatory-design.mdc`**.
- **Web / JS / TS:** route every UI string through the project i18n dictionary/helper (`src/lib/i18n/…` or equivalent). See **`web-frontend.mdc`**.

## Commit Messages

- Write all commit messages in English (see **`git-commits.mdc`**).
